# Markdown style

Source of truth: `../THE-NEXUS/04-STANDARDS/code-style/markdown.md` and `../THE-NEXUS/04-STANDARDS/documentation-standards.md`.

## Vault frontmatter (required for vault notes)

```yaml
---
created: YYYY-MM-DD
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: [tag1, tag2]
status: canonical | draft | archived
related: ["[[wikilink-1]]"]
---
```

## File header (required HTML comment)

```html
<!--
FILE: relative/path/from/vault-root.md
PURPOSE: One line, what this file is.
-->
```

## Style

- One H1 per file. Skip-levels are forbidden.
- `[[wikilinks]]` for vault-internal references; markdown links for external URLs.
- Fenced code with language tag. Always.
- Mermaid is the diagram default.
- Tables for tabular data; bullets for unordered enumerations; numbers for ordered procedures.
- One "last verified: YYYY-MM-DD" recency marker for time-sensitive content.

## Forbidden

- Emojis in vault content (operator preference; default: avoid unless the project explicitly allows them).
- Marketing tone ("Welcome to ...", "Easy!", "Just ...").
- Trailing whitespace (except markdown line breaks).
- Multiple consecutive blank lines.
- "TODO" without a date and an owner.

## Confidence levels for AI-authored claims

Mark explicitly:

- "Confirmed via X" - you read the source.
- "Inferred from Y" - you reasoned from another source.
- "Speculative" - you guessed; loud or remove.
